window.NL_MOD=window.NL_MOD||{};NL_MOD["l01"]={"id":"l01","kind":"les","les":1,"lvl":"A2+","title":"Onregelmatige werkwoorden 1","en":"Irregular past: the top 16","goals":["Recognise irregular past forms in a text","Know the past of the 16 most common irregular verbs, singular and plural","Tell what you did on a day in the past"],"discover":{"title":"Een rare maandag","intro":"Listen and read. The highlighted words are all past tense. Look at them: what's different from *werkte* and *woonde* (Module 5)?","text":"Vorige maandag ==was== een rare dag. Ik ==had== een afspraak in Utrecht, dus ik ==ging== met de trein. Op het station ==zag== ik dat er een storing ==was==. Ik ==stond== een halfuur op het perron.\n\nToen ==kwam== er eindelijk een trein, maar die ==was== heel druk. Ik ==kon== niet zitten, dus ik ==moest== staan. Een man naast mij ==zei==: 'Dit gebeurt elke week!'\n\nIn Utrecht ==nam== ik de bus. Ik ==kwam== twintig minuten te laat. Mijn collega ==wist== het al: zij ==zat== in dezelfde trein! Ze ==deed== de deur open en lachte.\n\n's Avonds ==bleef== ik lekker thuis. Ik ==kreeg== een berichtje van NS: 'Excuses voor de vertraging.' Gelukkig ==reed== de trein de volgende dag weer op tijd.","qs":[{"t":"mc","q":"The highlighted words are all…","o":["past forms of verbs","present forms of verbs","participles (ge-…)"],"a":0},{"t":"tf","q":"These past forms end in -te or -de, like *werkte* and *woonde*.","a":false,"x":"They don't. These verbs change their **vowel** (and sometimes more) instead of adding -te/-de. That's why they're called **irregular**."},{"t":"mc","q":"*ging* is the past of…","o":["gaan","geven","gooien"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"*kwam* is the past of…","o":["komen","kunnen","kammen"],"a":0}],"au":"audio/l01/disc.m4a"},"chunks":[{"title":"Regelmatig of onregelmatig?","explain":"In Module 5 you learned the **regular** past: stem + -te/-de (*werkte, woonde*). The most common verbs don't follow that rule: they **change their vowel**. Dutch has about 150 of them, but **16** cover most of what you say every day. Today: those 16.\n\nThe four most important:\n\n| infinitive | ik / jij / u / hij / zij | wij / jullie / zij |\n|---|---|---|\n| zijn (to be) | ==was== | waren |\n| hebben (to have) | ==had== | hadden |\n| gaan (to go) | ==ging== | gingen |\n| komen (to come) | ==kwam== | kwamen |\n\n- There is **one form for all singular persons**: *ik was, jij was, u was, hij was*. No -t!\n- The plural (*wij, jullie, zij* = they) has its own form.","items":[{"t":"type","q":"**Gisteren _____ ik erg moe.** (zijn)","a":["was"]},{"t":"type","q":"**We _____ geen tijd.** (hebben)","a":["hadden"]},{"t":"mc","q":"Vorige week _____ ik met de trein. (gaan)","o":["ging","gaade","gaat"],"a":0,"keep":true},{"t":"type","q":"**Hij _____ te laat.** (komen)","a":["kwam"],"x":"One form for all singular persons: *ik kwam, jij kwam, hij **kwam***."}]},{"title":"Zien, doen, nemen, staan, zitten","explain":"| infinitive | singular | plural |\n|---|---|---|\n| zien (to see) | ==zag== | zagen |\n| doen (to do) | ==deed== | deden |\n| nemen (to take) | ==nam== | namen |\n| staan (to stand) | ==stond== | stonden |\n| zitten (to sit) | ==zat== | zaten |\n\n- *deed* has **two e's**, *deden* only one.\n- *stond* gets a **d** at the end: *ik stond*.","items":[{"t":"type","q":"**Ik _____ een storing op het bord.** (zien)","a":["zag"]},{"t":"type","q":"**Ze _____ de bus naar huis.** (nemen; *ze* = she)","a":["nam"]},{"t":"mc","q":"We _____ een uur op het perron. (staan)","o":["stonden","stoonden","staden"],"a":0,"keep":true},{"t":"type","q":"**Mijn collega _____ in dezelfde trein.** (zitten)","a":["zat"]}]},{"title":"De ij → ee-groep: rijden, krijgen, blijven","explain":"Many verbs with **ij** get **ee** in the past. Learn these three now; more of them follow in Les 3.\n\n| infinitive | singular | plural |\n|---|---|---|\n| rijden (to ride, drive) | ==reed== | reden |\n| krijgen (to get, receive) | ==kreeg== | kregen |\n| blijven (to stay) | ==bleef== | bleven |\n\n- In the plural, **f becomes v**: *bleef → bleven*.","items":[{"t":"type","q":"**De trein _____ weer op tijd.** (rijden)","a":["reed"]},{"t":"type","q":"**Ik _____ een berichtje van NS.** (krijgen)","a":["kreeg"]},{"t":"type","q":"**Wij _____ de hele dag thuis.** (blijven)","a":["bleven"],"x":"*bleef* → plural *ble**v**en* (f → v)."}]},{"title":"Kunnen, moeten, weten, zeggen","explain":"| infinitive | singular | plural |\n|---|---|---|\n| kunnen (can) | ==kon== | konden |\n| moeten (must, have to) | ==moest== | moesten |\n| weten (to know) | ==wist== | wisten |\n| zeggen (to say) | ==zei== | zeiden |\n\n- *kon* and *moest* often come with a second verb at the **end**: *Ik **kon** niet **zitten**. Ik **moest** **staan**.*","items":[{"t":"type","q":"**Ik _____ niet zitten.** (kunnen)","a":["kon"]},{"t":"type","q":"**We _____ staan.** (moeten)","a":["moesten"]},{"t":"mc","q":"Wat _____ hij? (zeggen)","o":["zei","zegde","zegte"],"a":0,"keep":true},{"t":"type","q":"**Ze _____ het al.** (weten; *ze* = she)","a":["wist"]}]},{"title":"Het meervoud","explain":"The plural is the singular **+ en**, with a few spelling changes. Learn them as pairs:\n\n| singular | plural |\n|---|---|\n| was | ==waren== (s → r!) |\n| had | ==hadden== |\n| zei | ==zeiden== |\n| kwam, nam, zag, zat | ==kwamen, namen, zagen, zaten== (one a) |\n| kreeg, reed, deed | ==kregen, reden, deden== (one e) |\n| bleef | ==bleven== (f → v) |\n| ging, stond, kon, moest, wist | ==gingen, stonden, konden, moesten, wisten== |\n\nUse the plural with **wij/we, jullie, zij/ze (they)** and with plural nouns: *De kinderen **waren** moe.*","items":[{"t":"type","q":"**Wij _____ te laat.** (komen)","a":["kwamen"]},{"t":"type","q":"**Jullie _____ geen tijd.** (hebben)","a":["hadden"]},{"t":"mc","q":"De reizigers _____ in de trein. (zitten)","o":["zaten","zatten","zatte"],"a":0,"keep":true},{"t":"type","q":"**De kinderen _____ moe.** (zijn)","a":["waren"],"x":"*was* → ***waren*** (the s becomes r)."}]}],"practice":[{"t":"mc","q":"Which one is a past form?","o":["kreeg","krijgt","krijgen"],"a":0},{"t":"tf","q":"*wist* is the past of *weten*.","a":true},{"t":"type","q":"**Vorige week _____ ik naar Amsterdam.** (gaan)","a":["ging"]},{"t":"type","q":"**Hij _____ niets.** (zeggen)","a":["zei"]},{"t":"type","q":"**Ik _____ hem niet op het station.** (zien)","a":["zag"]},{"t":"type","q":"**De kinderen _____ buiten.** (blijven)","a":["bleven"]},{"t":"type","q":"**We _____ een taxi.** (nemen)","a":["namen"]},{"t":"type","q":"Regular or irregular? **Gisteren _____ ik tot zes uur.** (werken)","a":["werkte"],"x":"*werken* is **regular** (Module 5): *werk-* ends in k → **-te**."},{"t":"type","q":"Regular or irregular? **Toen _____ de trein eindelijk.** (komen)","a":["kwam"],"x":"*komen* is irregular: **kwam**."},{"t":"type","q":"Make it past: **Ik heb geen tijd.**","a":["Ik had geen tijd."]},{"t":"type","q":"Make it past: **We moeten lang wachten.**","a":["We moesten lang wachten.","Wij moesten lang wachten."]},{"t":"type","q":"Make it past: **Ze krijgt een vergoeding.**","a":["Ze kreeg een vergoeding.","Zij kreeg een vergoeding."]},{"t":"order","q":"*Yesterday I went to Utrecht by train.*","a":["Gisteren ging ik met de trein naar Utrecht.","Ik ging gisteren met de trein naar Utrecht."],"x":"Time word first → verb next: *Gisteren **ging** ik …*"},{"t":"type","q":"Translate: *We could not sit, so we had to stand.*","a":["We konden niet zitten, dus we moesten staan.","Wij konden niet zitten, dus wij moesten staan.","We konden niet zitten, dus moesten we staan.","We konden niet zitten dus we moesten staan.","Wij konden niet zitten, dus we moesten staan."],"x":"*kunnen* → **konden**, *moeten* → **moesten**; the infinitive goes to the end."}],"words":[{"nl":"was","say":"zijn, was, waren","en":"past of zijn (to be) · plural: waren","ex":"Gisteren was ik erg moe.","cz":"was","au":"audio/l01/w0.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x0.m4a"},{"nl":"had","say":"hebben, had, hadden","en":"past of hebben (to have) · plural: hadden","ex":"Ik had geen tijd.","cz":"had","au":"audio/l01/w1.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x1.m4a"},{"nl":"ging","say":"gaan, ging, gingen","en":"past of gaan (to go) · plural: gingen","ex":"Ik ging met de trein naar Utrecht.","cz":"ging","au":"audio/l01/w2.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x2.m4a"},{"nl":"kwam","say":"komen, kwam, kwamen","en":"past of komen (to come) · plural: kwamen","ex":"De trein kwam te laat.","cz":"kwam","au":"audio/l01/w3.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x3.m4a"},{"nl":"zag","say":"zien, zag, zagen","en":"past of zien (to see) · plural: zagen","ex":"Ik zag een storing op het bord.","cz":"zag","au":"audio/l01/w4.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x4.m4a"},{"nl":"deed","say":"doen, deed, deden","en":"past of doen (to do) · plural: deden","ex":"Wat deed je gisteren?","cz":"deed","au":"audio/l01/w5.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x5.m4a"},{"nl":"nam","say":"nemen, nam, namen","en":"past of nemen (to take) · plural: namen","ex":"Ze nam de bus naar huis.","cz":"nam","au":"audio/l01/w6.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x6.m4a"},{"nl":"stond","say":"staan, stond, stonden","en":"past of staan (to stand) · plural: stonden","ex":"Ik stond een uur op het perron.","cz":"stond","au":"audio/l01/w7.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x7.m4a"},{"nl":"zat","say":"zitten, zat, zaten","en":"past of zitten (to sit) · plural: zaten","ex":"Hij zat naast mij in de trein.","cz":"zat","au":"audio/l01/w8.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x8.m4a"},{"nl":"reed","say":"rijden, reed, reden","en":"past of rijden (to ride, drive) · plural: reden","ex":"De trein reed heel langzaam.","cz":"reed","au":"audio/l01/w9.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x9.m4a"},{"nl":"kon","say":"kunnen, kon, konden","en":"past of kunnen (can) · plural: konden","ex":"Ik kon niet zitten.","cz":"kon","au":"audio/l01/w10.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x10.m4a"},{"nl":"moest","say":"moeten, moest, moesten","en":"past of moeten (must) · plural: moesten","ex":"Ik moest de hele reis staan.","cz":"moest","au":"audio/l01/w11.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x11.m4a"},{"nl":"wist","say":"weten, wist, wisten","en":"past of weten (to know) · plural: wisten","ex":"Ik wist het niet.","cz":"wist","au":"audio/l01/w12.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x12.m4a"},{"nl":"zei","say":"zeggen, zei, zeiden","en":"past of zeggen (to say) · plural: zeiden","ex":"Wat zei de conducteur?","cz":"zei","au":"audio/l01/w13.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x13.m4a"},{"nl":"kreeg","say":"krijgen, kreeg, kregen","en":"past of krijgen (to get) · plural: kregen","ex":"Ik kreeg een berichtje van NS.","cz":"kreeg","au":"audio/l01/w14.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x14.m4a"},{"nl":"bleef","say":"blijven, bleef, bleven","en":"past of blijven (to stay) · plural: bleven","ex":"Ze bleef de hele dag thuis.","cz":"bleef","au":"audio/l01/w15.m4a","aux":"audio/l01/x15.m4a"}],"write":{"type":"Use it","title":"Wat deed u?","task":"Kies één dag van vorige week. Schrijf 4 tot 6 zinnen: wat deed u die dag? Gebruik minstens vijf vormen uit deze les (was, had, ging, kwam, zag, …).","en":"Use at least five irregular past forms from this lesson, and one regular verb (-te/-de).","min":30,"max":70,"useful":["Vorige zaterdag was ik …","'s Ochtends ging ik …","Toen zag ik …","Ik moest …","Daarna kwam …","'s Avonds bleef ik thuis."],"check":["I used at least five forms from this lesson.","Plural forms with we/ze/jullie: *gingen, kwamen, hadden*.","A time word at the start → the verb comes next: *Toen **ging** ik …*","One regular verb with -te/-de (*werkte, wachtte, fietste*)."],"model":"Vorige zaterdag was ik vroeg wakker. Ik ging met mijn dochter naar de markt. Daar zag ik een oude collega. We stonden een halfuur te praten. Daarna nam ik de bus naar huis, maar ik moest lang wachten. 's Avonds bleef ik thuis en ik kreeg een leuk bericht van een vriend."}};
